# Delimited code fences in the demo

## Root cause

The demo pins a Zensical plugin release from before CSV and TSV lexers are registered. Its existing CSV example is rendered as a table, so the site does not show code fence highlighting.

## Change

Pin the first plugin and lexer releases that provide delimited fence highlighting. Add unflagged CSV and TSV code fences to the demo's code examples. Omit the tab-normalize extension from this demo build because it replaces literal TSV separators with spaces before the theme sees the fence.

## Scope

The package pins supply lexer registration to the whole site. Any page containing a CSV or TSV code fence uses the same theme path as these examples. The extension change applies to the whole demo and preserves literal tabs in code.
